---
const checks = [
  {
    title: 'It gets tested against your awkward calls',
    body: 'Before anything goes live we run it through the conversations that actually go wrong: the caller who changes their mind, the one who will not give a name, the one asking for something you do not do.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Every run gets scored, not eyeballed',
    body: 'Each simulated conversation is marked against a written rubric rather than a gut feel, so we can tell whether a change made it better or just different.',
  },
  {
    title: 'It fails on our time, not yours',
    body: 'Anything that cannot clear the bar stays switched off and gets handed to a person instead. We would rather it say "I will get someone to call you back" than guess.',
  },
];
---
<section class="rel">
  <div class="rel-inner">
    <div class="rel-copy">
      <span class="rel-eyebrow">Before it goes live</span>
      <h2 class="rel-title">We score our own work before it touches your customers.</h2>
      <p class="rel-lede">
        The risk with automating the front of a business is not that it fails loudly. It is that it
        quietly says something daft to a good customer and nobody finds out for a month. So we
        built the checking part first.
      </p>
      <p class="rel-note">
        These are our own internal tests, run by us against simulated conversations. They are how
        we decide whether something is fit to switch on, not a measure of how it has performed for
        anyone else.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="rel-list">
      {checks.map((c) => (
        <li class="check">
          <span class="check-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="check-title">{c.title}</h3>
          <p class="check-body">{c.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  @reference "../../styles/global.css";

  .rel {
    background: var(--color-brand-bg);
    padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .rel-inner {
    max-width: 1120px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.95fr) minmax(0, 1.05fr);
    gap: 3.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .rel-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  .rel-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.2vw, 2.35rem);
    line-height: 1.14;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-brand-ink);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .rel-lede {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: var(--color-brand-muted);
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .rel-note {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-brand-muted);
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 0.9rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-brand-line);
  }

  .rel-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.35rem;
  }
  .check {
    background: var(--color-brand-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-brand-line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.35rem 1.4rem;
  }
  .check-rule {
    display: block;
    width: 26px;
    height: 2px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--color-brand-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .check-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-brand-ink);
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    line-height: 1.32;
  }
  .check-body {
    font-size: 0.89rem;
    line-height: 1.58;
    color: var(--color-brand-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .rel { padding: 3.5rem 1.25rem; }
    .rel-inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
